            <ArticleTitle>Active inflammatory bowel disease and coronary artery dissection.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case of a young woman with flare-up of Crohn's disease, who had an acute myocardial infarction due to the spontaneous dissection of the left anterior descending coronary artery, is reported. The literature on this rare condition is reviewed and a mechanism postulated for spontaneous coronary artery dissection in inflammatory bowel disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
